<title>GERMANY: BASF, Potash ask govt to overrule Kali veto.</title>
<headline>BASF, Potash ask govt to overrule Kali veto.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chemical giant BASF AG said on Thursday that it and Canada's Potash Corp have asked the German government to overrule a cartel office block on the sale of its Kali &amp; Salz unit to Potash.</p>
<p>BASF had hoped to sell 51 percent of its Kali &amp; Salz unit to Potash Corp of Saskatchewan Inc, but the German cartel office blocked the sale, citing a possible dominance of the German potash fertiliser market.</p>
<p>BASF said it and Potash Corp had jointly asked the German Economics Minister Guenter Rexrodt to overrule the cartel watchdog's decision and allow Potash to take up the Kali stake.</p>
</text>
